Aberration (ab-uh-RAY-shun)
Meaning: something unusual or abnormal
Hindi: असामान्यता / विचलन
Example: The sudden snowfall was an aberration.*


Belligerent (buh-LIJ-er-uhnt)
Meaning: aggressive and hostile
Hindi: झगड़ालू / आक्रामक
Example: The belligerent man started arguing.*


Capricious (kuh-PRISH-us)
Meaning: changing suddenly and unpredictably
Hindi: चंचल / अस्थिर
Example: Her capricious mood confused everyone.*


Debilitate (de-BIL-uh-tayt)
Meaning: to weaken
Hindi: कमजोर करना
Example: The disease can debilitate the body.*


Enigma (ih-NIG-muh)
Meaning: mystery
Hindi: रहस्य / पहेली
Example: His behavior is an enigma.*


Fastidious (fas-TID-ee-us)
Meaning: very careful about details
Hindi: अत्यंत सावधान / नकचढ़ा
Example: She is fastidious about her work.*


Hackneyed (HAK-need)
Meaning: overused and unoriginal
Hindi: घिसा-पिटा
Example: The speech sounded hackneyed.*


Iconoclast (eye-KON-uh-klast)
Meaning: one who challenges traditions
Hindi: परंपरा-विरोधी व्यक्ति
Example: The writer was an iconoclast.*


Juxtapose (JUK-stuh-pohz)
Meaning: place side by side for comparison
Hindi: साथ रखकर तुलना करना
Example: The painting juxtaposes joy and sadness.*


Lethargic (leh-THAR-jik)
Meaning: lazy or lacking energy
Hindi: सुस्त / आलसी
Example: I felt lethargic after lunch.*

